Dear Erez,

I am applying for the (Senior) DevOps Engineer for Sovereign Cloud position. This role is listed at T2/T3, and I would be joining at T1, so I want to be upfront about that from the start.

What I bring is a strong foundation to build on: hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines, Docker, and Git-based workflows from my rotations at SAP, along with production tooling work such as a VS Code extension using TypeScript and the Language Server Protocol. As co-founder of NEXtickets, I have also operated a live product end-to-end, including infrastructure decisions and real production incidents, which gave me a concrete understanding of what reliable deployment automation and monitoring require in practice.

I have foundational hands-on exposure to Terraform from a university project, and I am comfortable with Bash and Python. Building and hardening the reference environment for a Sovereign Cloud region is exactly the kind of technically deep work I want to grow into, and I learn fast when working on real systems with an experienced team around me.

I finish my dual studies at DHBW Mannheim in September 2026 and hold an unconditional hire recommendation from SAP. I am also open to the security clearance process this role requires.

#v(2em)

Best regards,

#v(0.5em)

*Max Meinel*
